From 5cead2c21fd801b38ffa03f418c828e5ad201513 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kantimohanthy <kantimohanthy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 15:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: replace all remaining stubs with real, working
 implementations

Not tagged [Bob:*] -- Claude, not an IBM Bob session.

This closes the gap identified in the previous audit: storyboard
generation, watermarking, animatic export, and client-side encryption
were all either hardcoded stubs or completely disconnected. All four
are now real, end-to-end, and covered by tests (33 new tests, 258/258
total passing).

Encryption (client -> server, end-to-end):
- New services/crypto_utils.py: AES-256-GCM decrypt matching
  lib/crypto.ts's encryptFile() format exactly (salt||iv||
  ciphertext+tag, PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256, 100k iterations). Verified
  against a real WebCrypto-equivalent encryption round-trip.
- scripts.py: optional 'passphrase' form field triggers decryption
  before parsing. Omitting it preserves the original plaintext
  behaviour -- fully backward compatible.
- upload/page.tsx: real 'Encrypt before upload' toggle + passphrase
  field, wired to lib/crypto.ts's encryptFile().
- Caught and documented a real bug during testing: the parser
  dispatches on filename extension *after* decryption, so encrypted
  uploads must keep their original extension (script.txt, not
  script.enc). Frontend does this correctly; documented in
  scripts.py's docstring for anyone integrating directly against the
  API.

Watermarking (was NotImplementedError on both methods):
- watermark.py: embeds a C2PA-inspired JSON provenance manifest as a
  PNG tEXt chunk; verify() reads it back. Explicitly documented as
  metadata-based (survives re-saving, not lossy re-compression/format
  conversion) -- not a robust/cryptographic watermark, and not full
  C2PA (no signing, no manifest store), matching SECURITY.md's
  existing honest claim.

Animatic export (was a hardcoded 501):
- animatic.py: GIF export via Pillow (zero system dependencies).
  MP4 export via ffmpeg subprocess -- a real *system* dependency now
  documented in the module docstring; raises a clear AnimaticError
  (not a crash) if ffmpeg isn't on the host, so callers can fall back
  to GIF instead of hitting a mystery failure.
- animatic.py router: pulls frames from the new frame_store.py,
  returns a real playable GIF/MP4 as a base64 data URI. 404s cleanly
  if no frames were generated yet for the script.

Storyboard generation (was a hardcoded dummyimage.com URL):
- image_generation.py: added two concrete providers behind the
  existing ImageGenerationProvider interface --
  LocalPlaceholderProvider (offline, Pillow-rendered, clearly labeled
  'not AI-generated') and HuggingFaceProvider (real Inference API
  call, written to spec and unit-tested with mocks, but NOT verified
  live -- this sandbox has no network path to huggingface.co).
  get_default_provider() picks HuggingFace if HUGGINGFACE_API_TOKEN is
  set, otherwise falls back to the local placeholder so the pipeline
  always returns something real rather than a fake URL.
- generate.py: builds a CinematicPrompt directly from parsed scene
  metadata (deterministic, no LLM call required), generates via the
  selected provider, watermarks the result, stores the frame for
  animatic assembly, and returns a data URI. Response now includes
  provider_id so the frontend can honestly label placeholder vs. real
  AI output instead of implying live generation either way.
- New GET /api/generate/frames/{script_id} -- lightweight frame-count
  check used by Judge Mode.

Frontend (storyboard + judge pages now reflect real state):
- storyboard/page.tsx: per-scene 'Generate Frame' + 'Generate All',
  displays actual generated images, labels local-placeholder frames
  vs. real-provider frames, wires 'Export Animatic' to the real
  endpoint and renders the returned GIF inline.
- judge/page.tsx: polls real script/frame/budget state every 3s
  instead of every step being hardcoded strings. Introduced an
  'available' status (implemented, not yet exercised on this
  script) distinct from 'done' (verified for this script) and
  'pending' -- avoids falsely claiming per-script completion for
  capabilities we can't actually verify were used on that script.

Dependency fix:
- Bumped next 14.2.5 -> 14.2.35 (patch only, no major-version jump)
  to close a critical-severity CVE flagged by npm audit. The
  remaining 18 high-severity findings are all in the dev-only ESLint
  toolchain and require major version jumps (ESLint 8->10,
  eslint-config-next -> 16, which targets Next 16) -- left alone
  intentionally rather than risking a breaking upgrade 4 days before
  the deadline. Documented here for a deliberate follow-up decision.

Verified: 258/258 backend tests pass (33 new), ruff clean, tsc
--noEmit clean, next lint clean, full pipeline smoke-tested live
(upload -> generate x2 -> export gif -> export mp4 -> budget, plus
error paths). Production build still not verified in this sandbox
(no network for next/font's Google Fonts fetch) -- verify locally.
